    <bpmn:process id="W_W4363" name="W4363. Mystery Shopping &amp; Service-Audit Program Design &amp; Methodology" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Strategy (W4361); methodology review
Frequency: Annual design + continuous operation
Volume: One mystery-shop/service-audit methodology
Owner: Service Quality / Quality (VS-31)
Participants: Service Quality, CX (VS-13), Vendor (VS-34), Store Ops (VS-07), Risk (VS-21.2), Privacy (VS-91)
Source: workflow W4363 — Mystery Shopping &amp; Service-Audit Program Design &amp; Methodology</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4363_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4363_Lane1" name="Service Quality">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4363_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4363_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4363_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4363_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4363_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4363_Start3" name="Strategy (W4361); methodology review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4363_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4363_Task4" name="Service Quality design the methodology — scenario types (purchase, return…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Service Quality design the methodology — scenario types (purchase, return, complaint, inquiry, B2B quote, omnichannel), shopper profile (segment-realistic), randomized store/time/associate coverage, and frequency
Responsible (R): Service Quality
Accountable (A): Head of Service Quality
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4363_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4363_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4363_Task5" name="Service Quality/Vendor build the scenario scripts &amp; evidence-capture protocol…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Service Quality/Vendor build the scenario scripts &amp; evidence-capture protocol (what to observe, evidence type, lawfulness per W4367), and the data-validation/quality-control steps
Responsible (R): Service Quality / Vendor
Accountable (A): Head of Service Quality
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4363_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4363_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4363_Task6" name="Service Quality/Risk define anti-gaming/anti-collusion controls (variable…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Service Quality/Risk define anti-gaming/anti-collusion controls (variable timing, shopper rotation, no-notice, evidence verification W4381) and pilot before rollout
Responsible (R): Service Quality / Risk
Accountable (A): Head of Service Quality / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4363_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4363_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4363_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4363_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-163 (ensure service-quality audit independence.) | - CTL-668: methodology randomized &amp; evidence-based; anti-collusion controls (W4381); piloted before rollout
Owner: Service Quality / Quality (VS-31)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
